            <ArticleTitle>More exercise for the diabetics? Physical activity and prevention of ischaemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>71-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Epidemiologic studies suggest that a high level of physical activity would protect against coronary heart disease. There is accumulating evidence that habitual physical training may reduce some risk factors of atherosclerosis in both non-diabetic and in diabetic subjects. In this article the relationship of exercise to cardiovascular risk factors in diabetic patients is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
